================================================================================
2. STATUTORY LEGAL DISCLAIMER (ADVOCATES ACT, 1961)
================================================================================
Nyayi is an AI-powered Indian legal guidance, legal literacy, and educational
assistance platform. It utilizes machine learning models to synthesize and
explain Indian statutory codes, including the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS) 2023,
Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita (BNSS) 2023, Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam (BSA)
2023, and legacy Indian Penal Code (IPC) provisions in simple, understandable terms.

CRITICAL STATUTORY DECLARATION:
  (a) Nyayi is NOT a law firm and does NOT engage in the practice of law.
  (b) The responses and guidance provided by Nyayi do NOT constitute formal legal advice,
      advocate counseling, or court representation under the Advocates Act, 1961 or
      the Bar Council of India (BCI) Rules.
  (c) Use of this Software does NOT establish an attorney-client relationship.
  (d) Citizens and users facing ongoing litigation, police investigation, or critical
      legal proceedings are strongly advised to seek formal counsel from a certified,
      enrolled advocate or free state legal aid (NALSA/SLSA).

